I'm guessing you've heard all the usual tips:  play dwarven valk, get
poison, fire, cold, sleep and shock res (preferably without getting
crowned), all that stuff..

I'd say if you're dying to things that you know will kill you, you're
simply playing too fast.  Slow down between each move, it's not a real-
time race!

Also, your first ascension is probably going to be one where you find
a CoMR and speed boots in an armour shop beside a co-aligned altar on
DL 2 and minetown has 2 magic lamps and a wand of death.  So just keep
trying and a good game will come eventually.

Other tips I'd give are:
Really use that starting pet - get it to XL 9 and let it take out
minetown watchmen.  Free gloves!
Make more holy water.  Yes, even more.  I've never had too much holy
water, and most potions are probably not worth keeping.  Even if it's
just to bless your =3DoLev.
You'll also probably want to bless-genocide L.  So price-id all
scrolls, and only use ?oID to identify the 200 and 300zm ones.
If you're a valk, hang around the quest eating giant corpses until
you've maxed str and got shock res.
Oh, and polypile once you find a wand - even if you have only, say, 2
junk amulets, lev boots, =3DoIncreaseAccuracy and a handful of elven
boots and cloaks to burn, if you turn even one of those into speed
boots or a CoMR early, it can make life much easier.

Anyway, my 2 zm,

good luck!
